{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":76085,"duration_api_ms":76051,"num_turns":9,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"679bab7f-bf72-43be-9113-a9ce2b761d98","total_cost_usd":0.34506499999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29670,"cache_read_input_tokens":155945,"output_tokens":3265,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29670,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":3265,"cacheReadInputTokens":155945,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29670,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.34506499999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"rulings":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-540a2c8b","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment identifies a real pattern weakness in 2 of 3 migration tests, but the existing test suite already addresses it. The test at lines 199-203 explicitly removes `stability_tracker` from a serialized TankState to construct a genuine pre-v3 payload — this is exactly the pattern the amendment requests. Additionally, the documented migration contract (save.rs:47-48) requires adding a per-bump test, and all newly added TankState fields already use `#[serde(default)]`. The proposed generic regression test (removing an arbitrary field) is fragile, couples to current schema internals, and would need constant updating. The combination of the existing field-removal test demonstrating the correct pattern plus the mandatory per-bump test obligation provides adequate coverage. The remaining risk — that a future developer follows the weaker test pattern instead of the field-removal pattern — is a process concern better addressed by code review than by a perpetually-maintained regression test."}],"summary":"Rejected the single disputed amendment (fr-1-540a2c8b). While the amendment correctly identifies that 2 of 3 migration tests serialize current TankState with all current fields and merely relabel the schema version, the existing test at lines 199-203 already demonstrates the correct pattern by explicitly removing `stability_tracker` to simulate a true pre-v3 payload. Combined with the documented migration contract requiring per-bump tests and the consistent use of `#[serde(default)]` on all new fields, the current test infrastructure is adequate. The proposed generic regression test would be fragile and redundant with the per-bump obligation."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a132af68-62ae-475b-a6d4-6141d578a0cf"}
